scope closing the identity gap in the weave so two branches merge, booking the plant-that-plants-nothing red with its census, and bringing both living pins back under their bounds by folding rather than shaving
status GREEN -- three Rye witnesses build and run, three rish runners green with their controls, tame_style_check clean, width-check green, the spine gapless with no headline drift, both pins under bound -- re-proven at 514 on the lap that landed it
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- three want your word. The ANCHOR: two branches each inserting several lines still interleave line by line, and closing it wants an anchor per insert, which widens Diff -- a seam rather than a lap, and the head names it rather than claiming otherwise. The 94 CONTROLS: a plant aimed at a line that has moved is a plant that plants nothing, and 94 of them span every lane, so the fix is 94 edits or one shared helper the fixtures import. And the CARD: it held 46 bytes of slack after I folded a peer's closed account whole rather than shaving live ones, which is the accreting trade -- yet eight ships at 2,048 apiece do not fit beside the spine, and that arithmetic is the standing tax.
